// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/ml/train_hslm.t27 -- main() trains the whole 3-block HSLM of specs/nn/hslm.t27 on real
; tokens: straight-through shadow weights, LAMB, a warmup-cosine schedule, global-norm clipping,
; held-out evaluation, and MSLH checkpoints that are read back and compared byte for byte.
; Issue: gHashTag/t27#10372.
; WHAT IS REUSED, NOT COPIED: the forward pass (hslm_forward, hslm_block_forward, the sacred
; attention, the FFN, the VSA stream and its gate), the backward pass (hslm_backward: the exact
; gradient of the current position's cross-entropy, embedding included), cross_entropy, the TWN
; quantizer (nn/ternary_ste quantize_twn) and the checkpoint header and layout (nn/hslm_data
; write_header, parse_header, the section offsets). They are reached through `use`.
; THE MODEL: ctx 27, vocab 729, embed 243, ff 729, 3 blocks, 3 heads of 81. Every ternary matrix
; (Q, K, V, O, up, down per block, and the output head: 19 matrices; 18 block matrices hold 1771470
; trits and the 243 x 729 output head adds 177147, 1948617 trits in all) has an f64
; shadow; after every update the shadow is requantized with TWN (delta = 0.7 mean |w|, alpha = mean
; |w| over the kept entries), one alpha per matrix. The float parameters (embedding table 729 x 243,
; RMSNorm gains, FFN biases, output bias) are trained directly. NPARAM = 2130138 f64 in one flat
; vector, 30 segments.
; THE STEP: 66 windows of 27 tokens, starts drawn by a xorshift64 PRNG (pinned seed); per window,
; 27 forward positions; the loss is the mean cross-entropy of the last k positions, each against the
; token after it, k = loss_positions (default 27: every position; 1: the last position against the
; 28th token, the objective of the first run, kept to the bit). Each scored position runs its
; hslm_backward right after its forward, with d loss / d logits scaled by 1/k.
; Gradients are averaged over the 66 windows, clipped to global L2 norm 1.0, and handed to LAMB
; (beta1 0.9, beta2 0.999, eps 1e-6, decoupled weight decay 0.01 on the matrices and the embedding,
; none on gains and biases, trust ratio ||w|| / ||r|| per segment, clamped to 10, 1 when either norm
; is 0 -- trinity-training autograd.zig lambStepSlice). Learning rate: 1e-3, linear warmup over
; 2000 updates, then cosine down to 1e-6 at TOTAL updates.
; THE FILES (all little endian):
;   /tmp/hslm/train.tok, valid.tok  "HTOK", u32 version 1, u32 N, N u16 ids below 729 (input)
;   /tmp/hslm/train.cfg             optional, key=value lines of integers: steps, total, warmup,
;                                   eval_every, ckpt_every, seed, speed, resume, synth, eval_windows,
;                                   loss_positions (1..27, default 27), gradcheck (1: print the
;                                   gradient checks and exit), profile (1: time the parts of every
;                                   step and print them at the end; section 1 says how)
;   /tmp/hslm/ckpt_<step>.bin       MSLH: nn/hslm_data's header (magic 0x484C534D, version 1, step,
;                                   f32 loss = the last minibatch loss under the k-position
;                                   objective) and its layout, f32: output shadow (243 x 729,
;                                   row-major [in][out]), then per block shadow_up (243 x 729),
;                                   shadow_down (729 x 243), bias_up 729, bias_down 243.
;                                   4971796 bytes, the size of hslm_step_10000.bin.
;   /tmp/hslm/ckpt_<step>.state     the full resumable state, since MSLH holds no attention matrices,
;                                   embedding, gains or output bias: a 64-byte header ("T27S", version
;                                   1, step, nparam, rng u64, beta1^t f64, beta2^t f64, loss f64,
;                                   nseg) then the parameters, LAMB m and LAMB v, f64 each.
; Both files are read back after they are written and compared with what was meant to be on disk;
; any difference makes main() fail (assert, a nonzero exit). resume=<step> in train.cfg restarts
; from ckpt_<step>.state and continues bit-identically (same windows, same updates).
; EVERY EVAL_EVERY STEPS one line goes to stdout: step, the objective (last<k>), the step's minibatch
; loss under it and its exp (train_loss_last<k>, train_ppl_last<k>), the mean minibatch loss since the
; last line, the loss on EVAL_WINDOWS fixed held-out windows (evenly spaced starts in valid.tok) at
; the last position (valid_loss, valid_ppl: the first run's number) and over all 27 positions of the
; same windows (valid_full_loss, valid_full_ppl), tokens/s (66 x 27 tokens per step over the
; training time only), s/step, the learning rate and the gradient norm before clipping.
; SPEED, HONESTLY: speed=0 runs the reference kernels of nn/hslm.t27 as they are. speed=1 replaces
; four kernels by local ones with the same results: ternary_matmul as a branch-free axpy over the
; rows of W (bit-identical: same summation order per output, x * 0.0 adds +0.0 to a sum that is never
; -0.0), trit_int and outer_add branch-free, and ternary_matmul_t_add with four partial sums (the one
; kernel that is not bit-identical; it only runs in backward). speed=2 (the default) also skips work
; whose result nobody reads: the head at positions 0..25 and, in the last block at those positions,
; everything but the key and value that the last position attends to. Under loss_positions = k only
; positions 0..26-k are unscored, so k = 27 runs the full forward everywhere and skips nothing. speed=3 (#10849)
; computes the speed 2 window layer by layer over all 27 positions, so each ternary matrix and each
; gradient row is read once per window instead of once per position, with every sum in speed 2's
; order. The tests check that speed 1, 2 and 3 produce the same logits as speed 0 to the bit, and that
; speed 3 produces the same logits, loss and gradients as speed 2 to the bit. The model is not reduced.
; WHAT DIFFERS FROM THE ZIG TRAINER (trinity-training @ 3e9648c, run R5): f64, not f32; LAMB, not
; AdamW; one global clip, not per tensor; linear warmup + cosine to 1e-6, not the phi schedule; the
; embedding table and RMSNorm gains are trained (the trainer froze the table); the gradient is that of
; the k-position mean, each position's with earlier keys and values as constants (nn/hslm.t27
; section 5; the tests check it against central differences); alphas are recomputed by TWN, not
; learned; the VSA table is nn/hslm.t27's hash, not Zig's PRNG; the MSLH body floats are IEEE f32 casts (round to nearest even), the header loss is hslm_data's encode_f32.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module train_hslm;

use base::types;
use nn::hslm;
use nn::ternary_ste;
use nn::hslm_data;

; THE SHAPE. nn/hslm and nn/hslm_data both declare these five; a name two imports declare is not
; resolved, so this module declares them once, with the same type and value as both.
